@startuml CodexTopology
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
' purpose: the codex def's resolved topology — the harness layer, the seeded $CODEX_HOME, the loop, and the container boundary
' covers: defs/codex/**
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: internal/contract/image_size_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/config_set_test.go
' covers: e2e/codex_daemon_sync_test.go
'   how the harness is steered and gated _spec/defs/codex/codex-paradigm.puml
'   the empty-apt guard ................ _spec/defs/harness-image-layers.puml
'   what transient means to the sync ... _spec/packages/lib/config-seeding-and-persistence.puml
'
' ── CONFIG.TOML: THE KIT WRITES, PROVEO MERGES (2026-10-24, user: "Delete dup
' keys, merge the rest") ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED: on sbx, seed_codex_defaults never ran — proveo_sbx_passthrough
' exec'd past it (v2), and v3 launches the codex kit's ENTRYPOINT, not
' /entrypoint.sh. The kit's install hook rewrites config.toml on every create
' (approval_policy, sandbox_mode, mcp_oauth_credentials_store, and per auth mode
' forced_login_method + [model_providers.sandboxd]). So:
'   * approval_policy and sandbox_mode left defs/codex/defaults/config.toml;
'     the non-sbx path still launches with --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-
'     sandbox (entrypoint.sh), so nothing relied on the keys.
'   * proveo_merge_codex_defaults (entrypoint-lib.sh) inserts each missing
'     top-level default ABOVE the file's first [table] (below it, TOML would
'     read the key as the table's); CODEX_RESEED=1 resets those keys only. It
'     runs in proveo_seed after proveo_sync_config restore, and replaced
'     seed_codex_defaults's whole-file copy.
'   Pinned by internal/contract/codex_defaults_merge_test.go.
'
' ── NO DOCKER BINARIES OF ITS OWN (N14, DONE (wt) 2026-10-17) ──────────────
' codex was the one harness image Cut 4 missed: its Dockerfile still installed
' docker-29.7.2's static tarball and symlinked dockerd, shadowing the Engine
' proveo/base inherits from the sbx template. codex was absent from
' image_size_test.go harnessDockerfiles, so TestNoHarnessImageShipsDockerBinaries
' never read it. The user: "Delete the layer (Recommended)". MEASURED: the RUN
' is gone from defs/codex/Dockerfile, codex heads harnessDockerfiles
' (image_size_test.go:173-174), and the test was red before, green after
' (reported). The group, the start-docker LABEL (Dockerfile:47-50 since N26)
' and iptables stay — _spec/_devops/image-size-reduction.puml, Cut 4.
'
' ── NO APT LAYER OF ITS OWN (N26, DONE (wt) 2026-10-18) ────────────────────
' The image installs nothing through apt. Its apt RUN named no package: it
' paid an `apt-get update` and two cache mounts (proveo-codex-apt-cache,
' proveo-codex-apt-lists) for nothing, then ran `proveo-harden /usr /opt`.
' MEASURED: the RUN is deleted, and the file calls proveo-harden nowhere.
' base-node-lsp already runs that pass over /usr /opt, and only user and group
' edits sit between FROM and where the layer was (Dockerfile:13-41).
' internal/contract TestEveryAptInstallNamesAPackage now fails any tracked
' Dockerfile whose `apt-get install` names no package; it found opencode's twin.
' Image (MEASURED by the coordinator): rebuilt with the cache off, `docker
' history` shows no apt layer, and TestImageCodex passes.
' defs/codex/README.md's variants table now lists proveo/codex as the base of
' proveo/codex-browser; TestBrowserVariantsAreDocumentedAsALayerOnTheirHarness
' (internal/contract/browser_layer_test.go) refuses the old claim in any README.
'
' ── AUTH: THE LOGIN FILE IS A CREDENTIAL (moved from source, N14) ──────────
' Two ways in: a ChatGPT-plan login at $CODEX_HOME/auth.json, which the durable
' proveo home carries between runs, or OPENAI_API_KEY. With both present the
' login wins — codex's own default — and proveo withholds the competing key
' host-side for the same reason (_spec/internal/credentials/
' credential-decisions.puml: a login on disk out-ranks an env token).
' So the .codex home mount declares NO deny list — claudecode's posture, not
' cursor's. `codex login` writes ~/.codex/auth.json and a ChatGPT-plan run IS
' that file. Scrubbing it would make every subscription session log in again,
' and would hide the login from PersistedLogin, which is what stops proveo
' injecting a competing API key.
'
' ── codex-browser ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' defs/base-node-browser/Dockerfile applied onto proveo/codex (browserOf in
' internal/imagebuild/targets.go; _spec/defs/browser-layer.puml), so it is a
' strict superset: the language servers the entrypoint wires in as MCP servers
' are still there. Selected per run as the `browser` addon, never as a target
' of its own. (The manifest comment said FROM proveo/base-node-browser; that
' predates the layer-on-harness inversion and was not carried over.)
'
' ── APP-SERVER DAEMON STATE IS TRANSIENT (DECISION 2026-11-08) ─────────────
' Symptom on a Fedora host, codex 0.167.0 under sbx: "Error: daemon executable
' not found at /home/agent/.codex/packages/app-server-daemon/current/bin/codex;
' repair the existing installation, or run codex app-server daemon start…".
' MEASURED 2026-11-08 with the official @openai/codex@0.167.0 linux-arm64
' binary, a fresh CODEX_HOME and `codex app-server daemon start`:
'   packages/app-server-daemon/current   an ABSOLUTE symlink to
'       <CODEX_HOME>/packages/app-server-daemon/releases/0.167.0-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl,
'       a 392 MB release tree; siblings auto-update-version,
'       selection-history, install.lock
'   app-server-control/app-server-control.sock   a symlink to
'       /tmp/codex-daemon-1000/<hash>
'   app-server-daemon/daemon.pid   pid + bootId (VM-specific); also
'       daemon.lock, daemon-updater.pid, *.stderr.log
'   all three dirs absent   codex installs again from its own CLI ("Installing
'       daemon from CLI version 0.167.0 into …/packages/app-server-daemon...")
'   `codex features list`   daemon_auto_start stable true (on since 0.157.0)
' Root cause: _proveo_config_plan (packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh) lists source
' entries with `find -type f` and `-type d` only, so the config sync never
' copies a symlink. The .codex home mount carried the release tree and the
' selection files through ~/.proveo/.codex but never `current`, and the next
' sandbox restored a recorded install whose executable was missing.
' The Executor: "pick the option that makes it as close to `sbx` running codex
' natively". codex's daemon stays ON (no `--no-daemon`), and the .codex mount
' declares `transient: [packages, app-server-daemon, app-server-control]`
' (defs/codex/harness.manifest), so each sandbox installs its own daemon, as
' under native sbx. Transient never deletes: the host keeps any stale copy, and
' an operator may remove ~/.proveo/.codex/{packages,app-server-daemon,
' app-server-control} by hand.
' Rejected:
'   copy symlinks in the sync   absolute, per-VM links; 392 MB per save; the
'                               sync serves every harness
'   --no-daemon                 diverges from native sbx
'   daemon_auto_start=false     unverified against a recorded-but-broken install
' Pinned by internal/contract/config_set_test.go
' TestCodexDaemonStateNeverCrossesTheSandbox: red on the old manifest (5 leaks),
' green now.
' End to end, e2e/codex_daemon_sync_test.go (build tag e2e; a real codex ≥0.157
' from PROVEO_TEST_CODEX or PATH, else skipped) runs the real proveo_sync_config
' between two sandbox homes sharing one state dir:
' TestCodexDaemonStartsInEverySandboxAfterAHomeRoundTrip (the second sandbox's
' `codex app-server daemon start` succeeds; config.toml still round-trips) and
' TestCodexDaemonRoundTripWithoutTransientReproducesTheReport (transient cleared
' → "daemon executable not found at …/packages/app-server-daemon/current/bin/
' codex"; skips if a future codex repairs itself). MEASURED 2026-11-08, codex
' 0.167.0 linux-arm64: both pass, and the first fails with the operator's exact
' error when defs/codex/harness.manifest is reverted to 595b80af.
'
' ── NOTES BROUGHT INTO THE BOX (2026-11-08) ────────────────────────────────
' Every note below is 2-5 lines of at most 50 columns (TestSpecNotesFitTheBox).
' One fact changed in the rewrite: the Sandbox note said the posture is written
' "in BOTH places … on the argv, and in the seeded config.toml". That was stale
' since the 2026-10-24 section above (approval_policy and sandbox_mode left
' defs/codex/defaults/config.toml), so the note now says proveo sets the argv
' alone and, on sbx, the kit's install hook writes the keys.
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam ranksep 120
skinparam nodesep 80

left to right direction

title Codex CLI Topology — ML Blackbox Loop

actor "Human" as Human
actor "Codex CLI\n(codex)" as Codex

package "Harness Layer" as Harness {
 component "entrypoint.sh\n(docker)" as Entrypoint <<script>>
 component ".env loader\nOPENAI_API_KEY / auth.json check" as EnvLoader <<logic>>
 component "smoke-test mode" as Smoke <<mode>>
 component "steering detection\nAGENTS.md (native) | CLAUDE.md (fallback)" as Steering <<prompt>>
 component "verification discovery\nbuild / test / lint" as Verify0 <<logic>>
}

package "User Layer — $CODEX_HOME" as Home {
 component "config.toml\nkit: approval · sandbox · login · provider\nproveo: hide_agent_reasoning · doc fallbacks" as Config <<config>>
 component "AGENTS.md\nproveo house rules" as HouseRules <<prompt>>
 component "agents/*.toml\nread-only advisors\n+ spec-keeper (workspace-write)" as Subagents <<subagent>>
 component "[mcp_servers.lsp_*]\nmcp-language-server" as LspMcp <<logic>>
 database "sessions/**.jsonl\nrollouts — what `resume` reads" as Sessions <<db>>
 component "auth.json\n`codex login`" as Auth <<security>>
 component "packages/ · app-server-daemon/\n· app-server-control/\ndaemon state — transient" as Daemon <<storage>>
}

package "Execution Loop" as Loop {
 component "Spec / Goal" as Spec <<step>>
 component "Plan + Acceptance Criteria" as Plan <<step>>
 component "Implement (edit)" as Implement <<step>>
 component "Verify (run tests/lint)" as Verify <<step>>
 component "Inspect Failure → Adjust" as Inspect <<step>>
}

package "Container Sandbox" as Sandbox {
 component "codex --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\n(the container is the sandbox)" as Force <<flag>>
 component "/app workspace mount\nruns as host uid (non-root)" as Mounts <<storage>>
 component "network egress layer\nopen | allowlist | review" as Net <<security>>
}

cloud "OpenAI backend\napi.openai.com" as Backend

Human --> Entrypoint : starts container
Entrypoint --> EnvLoader
Entrypoint --> Smoke
Entrypoint --> Steering : report, never write
Entrypoint --> Verify0
Entrypoint --> Home : proveo_seed codex\n(merge missing keys)
Entrypoint --> Codex : " exec ""codex --dangerously-bypass-…"" "
Codex --> Config
Codex --> HouseRules
Codex --> Steering : reads project AGENTS.md
Codex --> Subagents : in-loop review gates
Codex --> LspMcp : code intelligence over MCP
Codex --> Sessions : writes each turn
Codex --> Daemon : daemon_auto_start\ninstalls from its own CLI
Codex --> Loop : executes loop
Loop --> Verify : runs detected commands
Verify -> Inspect : on failure
Inspect -> Plan : next iteration
Force --> Sandbox : within\ncontainer boundary
Codex -[#00BAC6,dashed,bold]-> Backend : inference
Auth ..> Backend : login OR OPENAI_API_KEY
Net ..> Backend : provider pin = "".openai.com""

note right of Home
  **$CODEX_HOME is $HOME/.codex, and proveo
  moves $HOME.** It sets ""HOME=/proveo-home""
  and mounts ""~/.proveo/.codex"" under it, so
  config, rules, subagents, the login and every
  transcript outlive ""--rm"".
end note

note bottom of Home
  **So ""CODEX_HOME"" is never baked into the
  image:** a build-time path resolves past the
  mount into the image's own home, discarded
  with the container. The entrypoint exports it
  once, so the CLI and every helper agree.
end note

note as CodexHomeSeed #F4F9FB
  **It resolves from the seed's home, not from
  $HOME.** ""proveo_seed"" writes where
  ""_proveo_agent_home"" points, preferring
  ""PROVEO_HOME"", while an sbx setup command
  runs as user 1000 with HOME from /etc/passwd.
end note

note as CodexHomeDrift #F4F9FB
  **A ""CODEX_HOME"" from the process's ""HOME""
  can name a directory the seed never wrote.**
  The session then starts with no config, rules
  or subagents and no error, so the entrypoint
  warns when an inherited value disagrees.
end note

note bottom of Subagents
  **Agents are TOML, not markdown.** The shared
  body arrives as a ""developer_instructions""
  VALUE, composed by ""render_subagents"" from
  one body per agent plus codex's frontmatter.
  Same bodies as every harness; other container.
end note

note right of Subagents
  **A multi-line LITERAL string, never a basic
  one:** literal strings process no escapes, and
  the bodies document backslashes on purpose. A
  basic string would eat them with no error, in
  a file nobody re-reads after composing it.
end note

note bottom of Sandbox
  **Codex's own sandbox is off, and not for
  cursor's reason.** Landlock+seccomp needs no
  unprivileged userns, so it could engage here;
  confining a disposable copy buys little, and
  an approval prompt stalls an unattended run.
end note

note right of Sandbox
  **""PROVEO_CODEX_SANDBOX"" turns it back on,**
  launching ""--sandbox <mode>"" with approval
  ""never"". proveo sets it on the argv alone:
  the seeded ""config.toml"" lost both keys on
  2026-10-24; on sbx the kit's hook writes them.
end note

note right of LspMcp
  **LSP arrives over MCP, as for cursor: codex
  has no external-LSP config.** proveo writes
  between ""# >>> proveo lsp"" markers, so an
  operator's own ""[mcp_servers.*]"" entries
  survive a re-run; only proveo's block changes.
end note

note bottom of LspMcp
  **It is APPENDED, and TOML needs every
  top-level key above the first table.** A key
  added below the marker would be read as the
  last generated table's, so operators add
  theirs above it.
end note

note bottom of Daemon
  **codex's app-server daemon state never leaves
  the sandbox that installed it.** The config
  sync copies no symlink, so the absolute
  ""current"" link never crossed, and the next
  sandbox restored an install with no binary.
end note

note right of Daemon
  **Transient, so each sandbox installs its own
  daemon, as native sbx does.** Copying the
  links would carry absolute per-VM paths and
  392 MB per save, in a sync every harness uses.
end note

note top of Daemon
  **The host keeps its stale copy until an
  operator deletes it.** Transient only declines
  to sync in either direction; unlike deny, it
  never deletes what an earlier proveo saved
  under ""~/.proveo/.codex"".
end note

@enduml
